/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 183 0 R
/T (This project presents a low-cost, voice-controlled AI assistant built on the ESP32-S3 microcontroller. An I2S MEMS microphone \(INMP441\) captures speech and an on-device wake-word engine \(ESP-SR\) waits for the trigger phrase.)
/E (This project presents a low-cost, voice-controlled AI assistant built on the ESP32-S3 microcontroller. An I2S MEMS microphone \(INMP441\) captures speech and an on-device wake-word engine \(ESP-SR\) waits for the trigger phrase.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 183 0 R
/T (The recorded audio is streamed over WiFi to a cloud AI service, which converts speech to text, generates a reply with a large language model and returns synthesized speech. The reply is played through an I2S amplifier \(MAX98357A\) and a speaker.)
/E (The recorded audio is streamed over WiFi to a cloud AI service, which converts speech to text, generates a reply with a large language model and returns synthesized speech. The reply is played through an I2S amplifier \(MAX98357A\) and a speaker.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 183 0 R
/T (The open-source XiaoZhi AI firmware forms the software base, and MCP tools allow the assistant to control appliances by voice. The result is a compact, affordable and extensible smart assistant.)
